<?nv
import data

method languages(): array {
    return data.benchLanguages()
}

method workloadName(map workload): string {
    return workload["name"]
}

method hasRun(map workload, string language): bool {
    return data.benchRuns(workload["name"]).has(language)
}

method isBest(map workload, string language): bool {
    var runs = data.benchRuns(workload["name"])
    return runs[language]["ms"] == data.bestValue(runs, "ms")
}

method measure(map workload, string language): string {
    return data.formatMeasure(data.benchRuns(workload["name"])[language]["ms"], "ms")
}

method workloadField(map workload, string field): string {
    return workload[field]
}
?>
<Layout title="Benchmarks" description="Twelve workloads implemented once in each language and run on the same machine." section="benchmarks">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[90rem] px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-50">Benchmarks</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-ink-400">{data.benchWorkloads().length()} workloads, implemented once in each language, run on the same machine. Every implementation prints the same output - the runner refuses to compare results that disagree. Times are the best of five runs and include process start; memory is the peak RSS of the child process.</p>
        <ul class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-1 text-xs text-ink-400">
            {#for language in languages()}
                <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="size-2.5 rounded-full" style="background: {data.benchColor(language)}"></span><span class="font-mono">{data.benchVersion(language)}</span></li>
            {/for}
        </ul>

        <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
            <section class="rounded-xl border border-ink-700 bg-ink-900/60 p-5" aria-label="Fastest">
                <p class="eyebrow">Fastest, wins across {data.benchWorkloads().length()} workloads</p>
                <dl class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-6">
                    {#for language in languages()}
                        {#if data.winsOf(data.benchWins("ms"), language) > 0}
                            <div><dd class="font-mono text-2xl font-semibold" style="color: {data.benchColor(language)}">{data.winsOf(data.benchWins("ms"), language)}</dd><dt class="text-xs text-ink-400">{data.benchLabel(language)}</dt></div>
                        {/if}
                    {/for}
                </dl>
            </section>
            <section class="rounded-xl border border-ink-700 bg-ink-900/60 p-5" aria-label="Leanest">
                <p class="eyebrow">Leanest, wins across {data.benchWorkloads().length()} workloads</p>
                <dl class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-6">
                    {#for language in languages()}
                        {#if data.winsOf(data.benchWins("mb"), language) > 0}
                            <div><dd class="font-mono text-2xl font-semibold" style="color: {data.benchColor(language)}">{data.winsOf(data.benchWins("mb"), language)}</dd><dt class="text-xs text-ink-400">{data.benchLabel(language)}</dt></div>
                        {/if}
                    {/for}
                </dl>
            </section>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-ink-700">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
                <caption class="sr-only">Wall clock time per workload and language</caption>
                <thead>
                    <tr class="border-b border-ink-700">
                        <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 eyebrow">Workload</th>
                        {#for language in languages()}
                            <th scope="col" class="px-3 py-3 eyebrow">{data.benchLabel(language)}</th>
                        {/for}
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    {#for workload in data.benchWorkloads()}
                        <tr class="border-b border-ink-800 last:border-0">
                            <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2 font-normal"><a href="#{workloadName(workload)}">{workloadField(workload, "title")}</a></th>
                            {#for language in languages()}
                                {#if hasRun(workload, language)}
                                    <td class="px-3 py-2 font-mono text-xs text-ink-400" class:font-semibold={isBest(workload, language)} class:text-primary-200={isBest(workload, language)}>{measure(workload, language)}</td>
                                {:else}
                                    <td class="px-3 py-2 text-ink-600">-</td>
                                {/if}
                            {/for}
                        </tr>
                    {/for}
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>

        {#for workload in data.benchWorkloads()}
            <section id={workloadName(workload)} class="mt-12 border-t border-ink-700 pt-10" aria-labelledby="h-{workloadName(workload)}">
                <h2 id="h-{workloadName(workload)}" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-50">{workloadField(workload, "title")}</h2>
                <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-400">{workloadField(workload, "description")} - every language prints <code class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-200">{data.benchOutput(workloadName(workload))}</code></p>
                <div class="mt-5 grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
                    <Chart title="Wall clock time" workload={workloadName(workload)} metric="ms" />
                    <Chart title="Peak memory (RSS)" workload={workloadName(workload)} metric="mb" />
                </div>
                <details class="mt-4" data-tabs>
                    <summary class="cursor-pointer font-mono text-xs text-primary-300">show the code</summary>
                    <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5" role="tablist" aria-label="Language">
                        {#for language in languages()}
                            <button type="button" role="tab" class="chip" data-tab={language} aria-selected={language == "novus"}>{data.benchLabel(language)}</button>
                        {/for}
                    </div>
                    {#for language in languages()}
                        <div data-tab-panel={language} hidden={language != "novus"} class="mt-3">
                            <Code code={data.benchSource(workloadName(workload), language)} lang={data.benchHighlight(language)} />
                        </div>
                    {/for}
                </details>
            </section>
        {/for}

        <section class="mt-12 border-t border-ink-700 pt-10">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-50">How to read this</h2>
            <div class="mt-4 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-sm text-ink-300">
                <p>These are microbenchmarks. They say something about the code a compiler generates for tight loops, allocation and standard library calls - and nothing about how a language feels in a large program, how good its tooling is, or how it behaves under a real workload.</p>
                <p>Times include process start, which is what a user waits for. That is the honest number for a command line tool and an unfair one for the JVM and Node, whose JITs need a long running process to pay off.</p>
                <p><strong class="text-ink-50">Where Novus does well:</strong> integer and float arithmetic, because the compiler proves which locals are numbers and emits plain C for them, and memory, because values are tagged pointers and objects are a single flat block.</p>
                <p><strong class="text-ink-50">Where it does not:</strong> sorting and allocation heavy code, where every element is still a boxed value behind a pointer, and hash maps, which store more per entry than a C++ <code class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-200">unordered_map</code>.</p>
                <p>Everything here lives in <a href="https://github.com/ezTxmMC/novus/tree/master/benchmarks" rel="noreferrer">benchmarks/</a> - sources, the runner and the raw results.</p>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>
</Layout>
